#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Fermions {#qiskit-fermions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`qiskit-fermions` extends the Qiskit SDK with tools for working on fermionic"
" systems. Within its scope it provides the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Efficient data structures for the representation and manipulation of "
"fermionic operators in different forms\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A framework for implementing operator conversion methods (including fermion-"
"to-qubit encodings)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A library of efficient implementations of common conversion methods\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A framework and library of gates for expressing fermionic circuits\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A transpilation pipeline integrated with the Qiskit transpiler process to "
"synthesize fermionic circuits into qubit-based circuits\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, `qiskit-fermions` integrates with other tools of the "
"ecosystem, such as:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) for the high-level ansatz"
" operators and efficient simulation of fermionic circuits (see [Relationship"
" to ffsim](#relationship-to-ffsim))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get started {#get-started}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Schematic description of Qiskit Fermions](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/overview.svg)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The schematic description in the image above provides a glimpse of the "
"breadth of features and general workflow that this package provides. You can"
" work in the fermionic regime with both, operator and circuit "
"representation, before you define a fermion-to-qubit encoding that plugs "
"into the multi-representation transpiler pipeline of Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of these features are explained in [several guides](/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/guides/overview) to help you get started. For an overview working "
"through exactly the pipeline shown above, start with the [1D Fermi-Hubbard "
"guide](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/1-d-fermi-hubbard).\n"
msgstr ""

