#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Technical discussion {#technical-discussion}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Design intentions {#design-intentions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This package is deliberately designed to align with Qiskit: it builds on a "
"core implemented in Rust and provides first-party language bindings to "
"Python and C. Its API intends to draw parallels to Qiskit in order to "
"seamlessly integrate into the workflows of users with experience in "
"programming Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A core principle to the design of `qiskit-fermions` was the decoupling of "
"its fermionic circuit representation from its qubitized form. To be more "
"precise: the fermionic circuits are meaningful by themselves and do not "
"require a mapping to qubit space to be interpretable. Furthermore, the "
"fermionic circuit representation cannot make any assumptions about its "
"fermion-to-qubit encoding applied later on. Consequently, while Jordan-"
"Wigner retains a dominant position and role, it is not assumed to be the "
"\\_default\\_ fermion-to-qubit encoding.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Relationship to ffsim {#relationship-to-ffsim}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and `qiskit-fermions` "
"divide the work rather than overlap. ffsim owns the high-level ansatz "
"operators and their fast simulation: it constructs a UCJ or UCCSD operator "
"from coupled-cluster amplitudes or a parameter vector, and simulates "
"fermionic states in a compact fixed-particle-number space. `qiskit-fermions`"
" owns the circuit side: it expresses that operator as a "
"[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") on fermionic modes and "
"transpiles it into a qubit circuit through *any* fermion-to-qubit "
"encoding.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That last point is the reason to bring an ffsim operator here. ffsim’s own "
"Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, so lowering "
"an ansatz through a different encoding (a local encoding trading qubits for "
"shallower circuits, for instance) is what this package adds. Conversely, "
"this package does not reimplement the ansatz math, so "
"[`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-"
"ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") and "
"[`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-"
"ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") take an ffsim operator directly as "
"their input.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the simulation side, ffsim is the backend. This package’s gates and "
"operators implement the protocol methods ffsim’s simulation functions "
"consume (`_apply_unitary_`, `_linear_operator_` and `_trace_`; see "
"[`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols "
"\"qiskit_fermions.protocols\")), so ffsim’s tools work on them natively, "
"with no conversion step. Building operators, mapping them and transpiling "
"the resulting circuits do not need ffsim at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the full picture, read the [ffsim relationship guide](/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/guides/ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Known issues {#known-issues}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As long as the Qiskit C API has not yet reached feature parity with its "
"Python API, some components of this package remain exclusive to its Python "
"API, too. This includes the entire circuit library "
"([`qiskit_fermions.circuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit\")) as well as transpiler passes "
"([`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler "
"\"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\")).\n"
msgstr ""

